---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Matthew Moore" description="Privacy Policy for the Matthew Moore consulting website."><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Privacy Policy'}]} /><section class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Effective date: {brand.effectiveDate}</p></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container prose"><p>This policy explains how this website handles information. It is written in plain language and may be updated as the site or services change.</p><h2>Information this website collects</h2><p>If you contact me by email or through a future contact form, you may provide your name, email address, and the details of your inquiry. The site may also collect limited technical information through analytics when analytics is enabled.</p><h2>How inquiries are handled</h2><p>Contact information is used to respond to your inquiry and communicate about a potential project. Please do not send sensitive personal, financial, or proprietary information unless it is necessary and appropriate to do so.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>Google Analytics 4 may be enabled to understand how visitors use the site, such as pages visited and general device or browser information. Google Analytics can use cookies or similar identifiers. Analytics is not loaded unless a Google Analytics measurement ID has been configured. The site is not intended to collect personally identifiable information through analytics.</p><h2>Third parties</h2><p>When enabled, Google may receive limited usage data through Google Analytics. Your email provider and any future contact-form service may process information you send to them. Their handling of information is governed by their own policies.</p><h2>Your choices and questions</h2><p>You can manage cookies through your browser settings. For privacy questions or requests concerning an inquiry you sent, email <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.</p><h2>Updates to this policy</h2><p>This policy may be updated to reflect changes to the website, its tools, or applicable practices. The effective date above will be updated when changes are posted.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
